## 8. S3 Glacier vs. S3 Standard vs. S3 Standard-IA

| Feature | S3 Standard | S3 Standard-IA | S3 Glacier Classes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Access pattern | Frequently accessed | Infrequently accessed | Rarely accessed / archival |
| Retrieval latency | Milliseconds | Milliseconds | Milliseconds to hours, depending on class |
| Restore request | No | No | Required for Flexible and Deep Archive |
| Storage cost | Higher | Lower | Generally lower for archival use |
| Retrieval charges | Depend on operation | Retrieval charges apply | Retrieval charges or restoration-related costs may apply |
| Typical use case | Website assets and active application data | Older files still needed quickly | Historical backups and long-term archives |

The key distinction is not just storage price. It is also how quickly the application needs the data and what it costs to retrieve it.

