## 9. Real-World Use Cases

### A. Application Log Archiving

A DevOps team collects application and infrastructure logs in S3.

Recent logs remain in an immediately accessible storage class for troubleshooting. Older logs transition to Glacier for long-term retention.

### B. Database Backups

A company retains recent database backups for fast recovery and archives older recovery points in Flexible Retrieval or Deep Archive.

The recovery plan must account for the time needed to restore archived backups.

### C. Compliance and Auditing

Organizations may need to retain records for years. Deep Archive can help reduce the cost of storing records that are rarely accessed.

Retention rules and legal holds must be configured according to applicable requirements.

### D. Media Archiving

Media organizations preserve historical videos, images, and production assets. Instant Retrieval can suit assets that occasionally need immediate access, while Deep Archive can suit rarely accessed originals.

### E. Disaster Recovery

S3 Glacier can store historical recovery data, but it should not be the only recovery mechanism for applications requiring very low recovery time objectives (RTOs).

Choose a storage class based on how quickly the business needs to recover.

