## 12. AWS CLI Examples

These examples demonstrate how to upload an object directly to a Glacier storage class, inspect it, and request restoration.

Replace bucket names, file paths, and object keys with your own values. Your AWS identity must have the required permissions.

### A. Upload an Object to Glacier Flexible Retrieval

```bash
aws s3 cp backup.zip s3://my-archive-bucket/backups/backup.zip \
  --storage-class GLACIER \
  --region eu-north-1
```

The `GLACIER` storage-class identifier means S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval.

### B. Upload an Object to Glacier Deep Archive

```bash
aws s3 cp backup.zip s3://my-archive-bucket/backups/backup.zip \
  --storage-class DEEP_ARCHIVE \
  --region eu-north-1
```

### C. Upload an Object to Glacier Instant Retrieval

```bash
aws s3 cp medical-image.jpg s3://my-archive-bucket/images/medical-image.jpg \
  --storage-class GLACIER_IR \
  --region eu-north-1
```

### D. Check an Object's Storage Class

```bash
aws s3api head-object \
  --bucket my-archive-bucket \
  --key backups/backup.zip \
  --region eu-north-1
```

Check the `StorageClass` and any restore-related fields in the output.

### E. Restore an Object from Glacier Flexible Retrieval

```bash
aws s3api restore-object \
  --bucket my-archive-bucket \
  --key backups/backup.zip \
  --restore-request '{"Days":3,"GlacierJobParameters":{"Tier":"Standard"}}' \
  --region eu-north-1
```

This requests a Standard restore and asks for the temporary copy to remain available for three days after restoration.

### F. Restore an Object from Deep Archive

```bash
aws s3api restore-object \
  --bucket my-archive-bucket \
  --key backups/backup.zip \
  --restore-request '{"Days":3,"GlacierJobParameters":{"Tier":"Bulk"}}' \
  --region eu-north-1
```

Deep Archive supports Standard and Bulk retrieval, not Expedited.

**Warning:** Do not upload important data to Glacier and assume it can be downloaded immediately. Flexible Retrieval and Deep Archive require restoration before normal access. Test the workflow with non-critical sample data first.

